  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Africa Church Advocacy programme is a new programme and part of a holistic programme across Africa with a regional/continental Church advocacy focus aimed to complement CAFOD&#x2019;s core programmes across Africa. To build a long-term flexible programme, with coherent partnerships, projects, and activities that contribute in an integrated and complementary way to achieve a cohesive pan-African goal, an extensive process of reflection, discussions, and engagement with partners and other stakeholders will be required.   In view of this and as part of the process of developing the Africa Church Advocacy Programme strategy, the following have been planned as key activities</narrative>
  </description>
